# Annotation isolation: two sibling functions each using @a should not cross-contaminate.
# f's @a and g's @a are independently scoped type variables — f can accept Int
# while g accepts String in the same dict without a type error.
[f: [fn [let x@a] x]
 g: [fn [let y@a] y]
 result: [f 42]]
=== out
["f": [fn [let x] ...]  "g": [fn [let y] ...]  "result": 42]
